  "description": "Erection of a rear loft extension with two dormers and 3no. rooflights at the front roof slope.",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed linked rear dormer roof extension, by reason of its scale, form massing, location and detailed design, comprises an&amp;nbsp;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-038383af-7fff-a2b9-aa46-885dfc2cbe90&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;incongruous, discordant and unsympathetic form of development &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;that is&amp;nbsp; out of keeping with the original building and wider terrace, resulting in harm to the significance of the site and fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Graham Road and Mapledene Conservation Area. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D1 (London’s form, character and capacity for growth) and D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) D4 (Good design) and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025)."
  ],
